<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Illtud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 500</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Saint Illtud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Illtud was a British abbot of around 500, founder of the monastic school of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llantwit-major">Llanilltud Fawr</a>, now Llantwit Major, in Glamorgan. Early saints' lives make him the teacher of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samson">Samson</a> of Dol, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gildas">Gildas</a> and other Welsh saints, and his school became a leading centre of learning in early Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/illtud.jpg" alt="Illtud" width="319" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gwenddwr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Illtyd_in_Holy_Trinity_Church,_Abergavenny.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
